---
title: "OpenAPI Compose deployment lifecycle"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Broken
    lg1: Serving
    lg2: Upgrade
    lg3: Provisioning
    lg4: Breaks OpenAPITrafficGated or PlannedRollRetainsCapacity
    lg5: Path to the OpenAPITrafficGated or PlannedRollRetainsCapacity bug
  }
  class lg0 pink
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 purple
  class lg3 blue
  class lg4 breaks
  class lg5 bugPath
  s0: Provisioning shared network
  s1: Unsafe traffic admitted
  s2: Provisioning Obot dependencies
  s3: Provisioning service authentication
  s4: Provisioning Obot
  s5: Provisioning Workers
  s6: Both stacks ready, traffic closed
  s7: OpenAPI traffic admitted
  s8: Rolling upgrade, capacity retained
  s9: Rolling upgrade, capacity lost
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: an OpenAPI request is admitted after every gate holds
  s0 --> s2: operator creates the explicit shared network
  s1 --> s0: the OpenAPI request completes
  s2 --> s0: the shared network disappears
  s2 --> s2: PostgreSQL starts
  s2 --> s3: PostgreSQL passes readiness
  s3 --> s3: service certificates are staged
  s3 --> s4: the service CA becomes trusted
  s4 --> s3: service authentication is withdrawn
  s4 --> s4: an Obot replica starts
  s4 --> s5: the Obot replica passes readiness
  s5 --> s5: a Worker starts on the trusted shared network
  s5 --> s6: the Worker passes readiness
  s5 --> s1: an OpenAPI request is admitted after every gate holds
  s6 --> s6: a Worker starts on the trusted shared network or the Worker passes readiness
  s6 --> s7: an OpenAPI request is admitted after every gate holds
  s1 --> s5: the OpenAPI request completes
  s1 --> s7: the Worker passes readiness or the Obot replica passes readiness
  s7 --> s6: the OpenAPI request completes
  s6 --> s8: a one-at-a-time Obot upgrade starts or a one-at-a-time Worker upgrade starts
  s8 --> s6: the upgraded replica is healthy again
  s8 --> s9: the Obot replica drains while another serves
  s8 --> s7: an OpenAPI request is admitted after every gate holds
  s9 --> s1: an OpenAPI request is admitted after every gate holds
  s7 --> s8: the OpenAPI request completes
  s7 --> s1: the Obot replica drains while another serves
  s1 --> s9: the OpenAPI request completes
  s9 --> s8: the Obot replica passes readiness
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  class s0 blue
  class s0 bugPath
  class s1 pink
  class s1 breaks
  class s1 bugPath
  class s2 blue
  class s2 bugPath
  class s3 blue
  class s3 bugPath
  class s4 blue
  class s4 bugPath
  class s5 blue
  class s5 bugPath
  class s6 blue
  class s6 bugPath
  class s7 teal
  class s8 purple
  class s8 bugPath
  class s9 pink
  class s9 breaks
  class s9 bugPath
